02:01 Yet the number of the children of Yisra'el shall be as the sand of the sea, which can't be measured nor numbered; and it shall come to pass that, in the place where it was said to them, You are not my people, it shall be said to them, You are the sons of the living G-D.
02:02 The children of Yehudah and the children of Yisra'el shall be gathered together, and they shall appoint themselves one head, and shall go up from the land; for great shall be the day of Yizre`el.
02:03 Say you to your brothers, `Ammi; and to your sisters, Ruchamah.
02:04 Contend with your mother, contend; for she is not my wife, neither am I her husband; and let her put away her prostitution from her face, and her adulteries from between her breasts;
02:05 lest I strip her naked, and set her as in the day that she was born, and make her as a wilderness, and set her like a dry land, and kill her with thirst.
02:06 Yes, on her children will I have no mercy; for they are children of prostitution;
02:07 for their mother has played the prostitute; she who conceived them has done shamefully; for she said, I will go after my lovers, who give me my bread and my water, my wool and my flax, my oil and my drink.
02:08 Therefore, behold, I will hedge up your way with thorns, and I will build a wall against her, that she shall not find her paths.
02:09 She shall follow after her lovers, but she shall not overtake them; and she shall seek them, but shall not find them: then shall she say, I will go and return to my first husband; for then was it better with me than now.
02:10 For she did not know that I gave her the grain, and the new wine, and the oil, and multiplied to her silver and gold, which they used for Ba`al.
02:11 Therefore will I take back my grain in the time of it, and my new wine in the season of it, and will pluck away my wool and my flax which should have covered her nakedness.
02:12 Now will I uncover her lewdness in the sight of her lovers, and none shall deliver her out of my hand.
02:13 I will also cause all her mirth to cease, her feasts, her new moons, and her Shabbatot, and all her solemn assemblies.
02:14 I will lay waste her vines and her fig-trees, whereof she has said, These are my hire that my lovers have given me; and I will make them a forest, and the animals of the field shall eat them.
02:15 I will visit on her the days of the Ba`alim, to which she burned incense, when she decked herself with her earrings and her jewels, and went after her lovers, and forgot me, says HaSHEM.
02:16 Therefore, behold, I will allure her, and bring her into the wilderness, and speak comfortably to her.
02:17 I will give her vineyards from there, and the valley of `Akhor for a door of hope; and she shall make answer there, as in the days of her youth, and as in the day when she came up out of the land of Mitzrayim.
02:18 It shall be at that day, says HaSHEM, that you shall call me Ishi, and shall call me no more Ba`ali.
02:19 For I will take away the names of the Ba`alim out of her mouth, and they shall no more be mentioned by their name.
02:20 In that day will I make a covenant for them with the animals of the field, and with the birds of the sky, and with the creeping things of the ground: and I will break the bow and the sword and the battle out of the land, and will make them to lie down safely.
02:21 I will betroth you to me forever; yes, I will betroth you to me in righteousness, and in justice, and in lovingkindness, and in mercies.
02:22 I will even betroth you to me in faithfulness; and you shall know HaSHEM.
02:23 It shall happen in that day, I will answer, says HaSHEM, I will answer the heavens, and they shall answer the earth;
02:24 and the earth shall answer the grain, and the new wine, and the oil; and they shall answer Yizre`el.
02:25 I will sow her to me in the earth; and I will have mercy on her who had not obtained mercy; and I will tell those who were not my people, You are my people; and they shall say, You are my G-D.  
11:01 When Yisra'el was a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Mitzrayim.
11:02 The more the prophets called them, the more they went from them: they sacrificed to the Ba`alim, and burned incense to engraved images.
11:03 Yet I taught Efrayim to walk; I took them on my arms; but they didn't know that I healed them.
11:04 I drew them with cords of a man, with bands of love; and I was to them as those who lift up the yoke on their jaws; and I laid food before them.
11:05 They shall not return into the land of Mitzrayim; but the Ashshur shall be their king, because they refused to return to me.
11:06 The sword shall fall on their cities, and shall consume their bars, and devour them, because of their own counsels.
11:07 My people are bent on backsliding from me: though they call them to him who is on high, none at all will exalt him.
11:08 How shall I give you up, Efrayim? how shall I cast you off, Yisra'el? how shall I make you as Admah? how shall I set you as Tzevoyim? my heart is turned within me, my compassion is aroused.
11:09 I will not execute the fierceness of my anger, I will not return to destroy Efrayim: for I am G-D, and not man; the Holy One in the midst of you; and I will not come in wrath.
11:10 They shall walk after HaSHEM, who will roar like a lion; for he will roar, and the children shall come trembling from the west.
11:11 They shall come trembling as a bird out of Mitzrayim, and as a dove out of the land of Ashshur; and I will make them to dwell in their houses, says HaSHEM.
12:01 Efrayim compasses me about with falsehood, and the house of Yisra'el with deceit; but Yehudah yet rules with G-D, and is faithful with the Holy One.  
12:02 Efrayim feeds on wind, and follows after the east wind: he continually multiplies lies and desolation; and they make a covenant with Ashshur, and oil is carried into Mitzrayim.
12:03 HaSHEM has also a controversy with Yehudah, and will punish Ya`akov according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.
12:04 In the womb he took his brother by the heel; and in his manhood he had power with G-D:
12:05 yes, he had power over the angel, and prevailed; he wept, and made supplication to him: he found him at Beit-El, and there he spoke with us,
12:06 even HaSHEM, the G-D-Tzva'ot; HaSHEM is his memorial name.
12:07 Therefore turn you to your G-D: keep kindness and justice, and wait for your G-D continually.
12:08 He is a trafficker, the balances of deceit are in his hand: he loves to oppress.
12:09 Efrayim said, Surely I have become rich, I have found myself wealth: in all my labors they shall find in me no iniquity that is sin.
12:10 But I am HaSHEM your G-D from the land of Mitzrayim; I will yet again make you to dwell in tents, as in the days of the solemn feast.
12:11 I have also spoken to the prophets, and I have multiplied visions; and by the ministry of the prophets have I used parables.
12:12 Is Gil`ad iniquity? they are altogether false; in Gilgal they sacrifice bulls; yes, their altars are as heaps in the furrows of the field.
12:13 Ya`akov fled into the field of Aram, and Yisra'el served for a wife, and for a wife he kept sheep.
12:14 By a prophet HaSHEM brought Yisra'el up out of Mitzrayim, and by a prophet was he preserved.
12:15 Efrayim has provoked to anger most bitterly: therefore shall his blood be left on him, and his reproach shall his L-rd return to him.  
13:01 When Efrayim spoke, there was trembling; he exalted himself in Yisra'el; but when he offended in Ba`al, he died.
13:02 Now they sin more and more, and have made them molten images of their silver, even idols according to their own understanding, all of them the work of the craftsmen: they say of them, Let the men who sacrifice kiss the calves.
13:03 Therefore they shall be as the morning cloud, and as the dew that passes early away, as the chaff that is driven with the whirlwind out of the threshing floor, and as the smoke out of the chimney.
13:04 Yet I am HaSHEM your G-D from the land of Mitzrayim; and you shall know no god but me, and besides me there is no savior.
13:05 I did know you in the wilderness, in the land of great drought.
13:06 According to their pasture, so were they filled; they were filled, and their heart was exalted: therefore have they forgotten me.
13:07 Therefore am I to them as a lion; as a leopard will I watch by the way;
13:08 I will meet them as a bear that is bereaved of her whelps, and will tear the covering of their heart; and there will I devour them like a lioness; the wild animal shall tear them.
13:09 It is your destruction, Yisra'el, that you are against me, against your help.
13:10 Where now is your king, that he may save you in all your cities? and your judges, of whom you said, Give me a king and princes?
13:11 I have given you a king in my anger, and have taken him away in my wrath.
13:12 The iniquity of Efrayim is bound up; his sin is laid up in store.
13:13 The sorrows of a travailing woman shall come on him: he is an unwise son; for it is time he should not stay in the place of the breaking forth of children.
13:14 I will ransom them from the power of She'ol; I will redeem them from death: death, where are your plagues? She'ol, where is your destruction? repentance shall be hid from my eyes.
13:15 Though he be fruitful among his brothers, an east wind shall come, the breath of HaSHEM coming up from the wilderness; and his spring shall become dry, and his fountain shall be dried up: he shall make spoil of the treasure of all goodly vessels.
14:01 Shomron shall bear her guilt; for she has rebelled against her G-D: they shall fall by the sword; their infants shall be dashed in pieces, and their women with child shall be ripped up.  
14:02 Yisra'el, return to HaSHEM your G-D; for you have fallen by your iniquity.
14:03 Take with you words, and return to HaSHEM: tell him, Take away all iniquity, and accept that which is good: so will we render as bulls the offering of our lips.
14:04 Ashshur shall not save us; we will not ride on horses; neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, You are our gods; for in you the fatherless finds mercy.
14:05 I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely; for my anger is turned away from him.
14:06 I will be as the dew to Yisra'el; he shall blossom as the lily, and cast forth his roots as Levanon.
14:07 His branches shall spread, and his beauty shall be as the olive-tree, and his smell as Levanon.
14:08 Those who dwell under his shadow shall return; they shall revive as the grain, and blossom as the vine: the scent of it shall be as the wine of Levanon.
14:09 Efrayim shall say, What have I to do any more with idols? I have answered, and will regard him: I am like a green fir-tree; from me is your fruit found.
14:10 Who is wise, that he may understand these things? prudent, that he may know them? for the ways of HaSHEM are right, and the just shall walk in them; but transgressors shall fall therein.  
